    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a search profile for a new CEO for one of our global tech clients. We need to really nail down the 'executive presence' requirements for this role. Can you give me a breakdown of the key personality traits and communication styles that someone needs to have to project commanding authority and leadership at the C-suite level?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly. The ideal prospective CEO will embody decisive and confident leadership qualities. They should exhibit a steady demeanor that underpins their authority; exuding competence without being perceived as intimidating. Communication should be clear, concise, and persuasive yet approachable, demonstrating both strategic thought and genuine engagement with stakeholders. They must inspire confidence and foster a vision that resonates with employees, investors, and the market. Adaptability and resilience, coupled with a strong sense of integrity and accountability, will further cement their executive presence. Finally, a comfortable but not overly informal rapport will help them effectively relate to the C-suite and the broader organization.",
