    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The distinction between the 'lion' and the 'wise leader' is interesting. My client is looking for someone who can truly command a global room, though. \n\nI'm curious about the practical application here—when we're evaluating these 'archetypes' or those specific vocal and physical traits, how do they impact the perception of 'natural' leadership? For instance, if we have a candidate whose communication style or physical mannerisms lean more towards those Eastern or non-Western archetypes you mentioned, would they be perceived as having the same level of 'command' or 'authority' in a traditional Western corporate boardroom compared to someone who fits the Western 'lion' model? I want to make sure we aren't overlooking talent just because their presence feels different.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
